cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data, or results, cite the accompanying manuscript and this repository."
title: "Radius-valley age evolution around cool stars: an inconclusive calibrated gate and a quantified path forward"
authors:
  - family-names: Shaad
    given-names: Zubayer Hasan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-2322-8553"
  - family-names: Al Abrar
    given-names: Md Mahdin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9645-152X"
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zabdax/radius-valley-age-evolution"
abstract: "A calibrated null/signal injection gate applied to the radius-valley age-evolution question around cool stars (Teff < 4200 K), with an FGK control, a 15-cell power grid, a power-versus-effect curve, and an external TIME Table age-ordering check. The verdict is inconclusive; both samples lack the power to discriminate a literature-sized effect from no effect."
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - radius valley
  - cool stars
  - M dwarf stars
  - astrostatistics
